course: dictionary
lesson: 3250
title: Epilepsy and seizures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Epilepsy is a condition of the brain. «Many classmates live with long-term conditions, epilepsy, cystic fibrosis, ADHD, heart problems, and none of them is catching or anyone's fault.» So epilepsy lasts a long time, you cannot catch it, and it is not anyone's fault.
explain: A seizure, also called a fit, is «a sudden burst of electrical activity in the brain that can make the body shake.» People who have epilepsy get seizures again and again. After a seizure, people usually recover, which means they slowly feel better and come round.
explain: If you see someone having a seizure, stay calm, call an adult, and move hard things out of the way. Cushion their head, time the seizure, and do not hold them down. Never put anything in their mouth.
fact: Epilepsy is a condition of the brain that makes a person have seizures (fits).
fact: A seizure happens when the brain's signals get mixed up for a short time.
fact: Some seizures are triggered by flashing lights.
fact: Nothing should be put in the mouth during a seizure, and nobody can swallow their tongue.
exercise: «Epilepsy is a condition of the brain that makes a person have seizures.» What is epilepsy? | *A condition of the brain that can cause seizures, or fits | A cold that is passed from person to person | A broken bone that heals slowly | A kind of fever that only babies get
exercise: Your friend has a seizure in the playground. What should you do first? | Hold them down so they stay still | *Stay calm, time it and call an adult | Put a spoon in their mouth to stop them biting | Pour water over their face
exercise: «Many classmates live with long-term conditions, epilepsy, cystic fibrosis, ADHD, heart problems.» Is epilepsy catching? | Yes, but only in winter | Yes, you can catch it from a classmate | *No, it is not catching and it is nobody's fault | Yes, if you touch someone's hands
test: What does «seizure» mean? | A kind of sweet | Lights that flash slowly | *A sudden burst of electrical activity in the brain that can make the body shake | A long holiday with friends
test: Why should nothing go in the mouth of someone having a seizure? | Because food is not allowed in the room | *Because it can hurt them, and nobody can swallow their tongue | Because it makes the seizure last longer | Because the mouth must stay dry
exam: «Febrile seizures, or fever fits, are scary but almost always harmless and don't mean epilepsy.» What does this tell you? | Fever fits only happen to adults | *Fever fits are not the same as epilepsy, and are usually harmless | Fever fits are the same as epilepsy | Fever fits are always dangerous and never harmless
